+# Actual development node Avalanche checks
+
+Run with a built native `lotusd` and an explicit development manifest:
+
+```
+python3 src/lotus_v2/node_avalanche_test/check_node.py --node /path/to/lotusd --manifest /path/to/manifest.json
+```
+
+The script uses fresh temporary homes and ephemeral loopback ports. It checks
+optional disabled mode, two actual observer peers, explicit minimum-height IBD,
+quorum evidence remaining absent without proofs, safe public persistence and
+private credential rejection (including symlink, FIFO, oversized and permissive
+files). It requires an easy-PoW manifest whose genesis is in the past and whose
+body limit fits 2MiB. No signing keys or production datadirs are used.
+
+Proof ownership, the 2016-confirmation boundary, 8-neighbor discovery, native
+quorum readiness and confidence128 finality need the separate funded nine-node
+fixture. These process checks do not claim that coverage. The existing peer and
+driver component suites cover authenticated transcript/signature validation and
+proof-only backpressure. Mixed inventory is demultiplexed by the actual node;
+transaction notices are consumed once before a retained proof-only retry.
